submission_format:
Return a JSON object with the same keys and nesting as the example below.

```json
{
  "artifacts": {
    "run_log": "/workspace/output/run.jsonl"
  },
  "results": {
    "heat_capacity": 0.0
  }
}
```

Units: heat_capacity in eV/(atom K).

Use the format below for the file `/workspace/output/run.jsonl`:
JSONL, one record per production sample from all seven forward stages. stage_index is 0..6 for targets 300,400,500,600,700,800,900 K; only stages 0..4 enter the heat-capacity fit; phase is "production". temperature_K is measured temperature in K and energy_eV_per_atom is total potential plus kinetic energy per atom.
```text
{"type":"sample","stage_index":0,"phase":"production","temperature_K":300.0,"energy_eV_per_atom":-3.65}
```
